      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2002 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "We present a case of a 38-year-old patient with angina after direct current (DC) cardioversion. The patient's medical history included documented coronary heart disease with interventional treatment of the LAD and RCA followed by emergency CABG 6 months ago. On recent admission, the coronary angiography revealed a giant pseudoaneurysm of the left descending coronary artery complicated by compression of LIMA. The pseudoaneurysm was successfully treated with three stent grafts."
      },
